{
  "$meta": {
    "name": "Cadence Design Tokens",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "spec": "docs/13-master-design-system-prompt.md (P5 tokens, P6 color, P7 type, P8 spacing, P9 icons, P10 motion, P23 theming)",
    "layering": "global -> alias -> semantic -> component",
    "conventions": {
      "colorFormat": "semantic colors are stored as HSL triples 'H S% L%' because shadcn/ui primitives consume them via hsl(var(--token)). global + component colors are hex or rgba.",
      "cssVariableNaming": "unprefixed. shadcn/ui hard-requires --sidebar-width, --button-outline, --badge-outline, --spacing-4 and all --radix-* to be unprefixed; a --cad- prefix cannot be applied to the shadcn contract set.",
      "themes": ["light", "dark", "high-contrast"],
      "defaultTheme": "dark"
    },
    "assumptions": [
      "ASSUMPTION: dark remains the default theme to preserve current shipped appearance; light is opt-in via [data-theme='light'].",
      "ASSUMPTION: the previously-undefined surface colors found during the 2026-09-30 audit (#18181B, #262628, #141416, #111113, #242428, #323236, #151518, #0E0E10) are promoted here to a coherent surface ramp rather than left as ad-hoc values.",
      "ASSUMPTION: the three coexisting indigos (#5E5CE6, #7A78FF, #7D7AFF) resolve to P6.1's values. #5E5CE6 measured 3.36:1 on dark surfaces and fails as text; P6.1 already specifies #7D7AFF for dark.",
      "TEXT-SAFE BRAND COLOURS: a saturated brand fill is not automatically a legal text colour. --primary measured 2.14:1 as text on a white card and --ai-fill measured 3.16:1, because both are fills chosen to sit behind a contrasting label. --primary-text and --ai-text exist for that: text uses the darker member of the same hue family (#A64B00 and #3634A3 in light) while bg-primary and bg-ai keep the saturated fill. Mixing the two in one component is the defect, not the token."
    ]
  },

